What are the lessons Beta gives Alpha like? I'm sure they're totally unlike=
=20
classroom lessons, because they're one-on-one and they're both kids.

I get a ride to church with a Mexican, and sometimes he asks me questions=
=20
like "=BFQu=E9 es la diferencia entre morir y te=F1ir?" ("zo mrobi'o cu fri=
ca zo=20
skagau ma?"), and I have to think for a few seconds, because the question=
=20
makes no sense until I realize he's asking about the English words. There a=
re=20
no differently spelled homophones in Lojban, but there are some minimal pai=
rs=20
and words differing by exchanging two sounds. So Alpha could ask Beta "What=
's=20
the difference between soda and egg?" or "Which is the rat and which is the=
=20
rabbit, again?"

Another possibility is that Beta could teach Alpha a tonguetwister and Alph=
a=20
asks what the words mean. So Beta says "le xruki le ginxre xrixruba xu xrul=
a=20
cu xrani" and Alpha asks what "xrixruba" is, or what "xu" means when it's=
=20
inside a tanru.

Pierre
